Package: datamatch
Title: Fetch Ocean Data from Several Sources and Match It in Space and Time
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Camille", "Ross", email = "camille.ross@maine.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-1428-2294"))
Description: Downloads ocean and atmosphere data and joins it to point data in
    space and time, at the downloaded data's own resolution. The join is a
    general spatiotemporal nearest-feature match, so either side may be species
    observations, survey stations, tag positions, or another gridded product.
    Four sources are covered behind one interface and one set of variable names,
    so a covariate arrives in a column of the same name whichever supplied it:
    the Copernicus Marine Service
    (<https://marine.copernicus.eu/access-data/>) for global reanalysis,
    analysis-and-forecast, satellite ocean colour and surface wind; HYCOM for an
    independent global model publishing sea-floor fields; FVCOM for
    unstructured-mesh coastal models such as NECOFS, or any other FVCOM output;
    and CCMP for a long six-hourly surface wind record. Variables are requested
    by familiar names such as 'SST' rather than product-specific codes, over
    monthly, daily, named-date or sub-daily steps, in parallel and cached. Also
    provides spatial and temporal resampling for combining products of different
    resolution, gap filling for satellite ocean colour, seafloor terrain from
    NOAA ETOPO, basin-scale climate indices, and plots for inspecting what was
    downloaded. Values sharing a name across sources are not interchangeable,
    and the documentation says so where it matters.
